WEBVTT

00:01.230 --> 00:04.100
<i>A new rival appears in front of Tsubasa.</i>

00:04.100 --> 00:06.380
<i>His name is Shun Nitta.</i>

00:06.380 --> 00:08.040
<i>A player with tremendous strength,</i>

00:08.040 --> 00:13.570
<i>his powerful, self-styled Falcon Shot was shocking, even to Tsubasa.</i>

00:13.570 --> 00:18.950
<i>However, Nankatsu's starters continued to
practice as usual, paying him no mind.</i>

00:18.950 --> 00:23.920
<i>Tsubasa is troubled by their attitude,
and urges them to train harder as a result.</i>

00:23.920 --> 00:25.580
All right! Let's do this!

00:25.580 --> 00:29.130
<i>Tsubasa's feelings resonated with Ishizaki and the others,</i>

00:29.130 --> 00:32.670
<i>bringing back the solidarity of Nankatsu Middle School.</i>

00:32.670 --> 00:36.140
<i>On the other side, Urabe's
Otomo Middle School continues to prepare,</i>

00:36.140 --> 00:38.680
<i>aiming for the reigning champion, Tsubasa.</i>

00:38.680 --> 00:40.740
<i>And finally...</i>

00:40.740 --> 00:46.560
<i>Shizuoka Prefectural Tournament begins, with a ticket to the National Middle School Football Tournament at stake.</i>

00:46.560 --> 00:53.320
<i>While aiming for the first three-time repeat in history, Nankatsu and Otomo are the top seeds of their respective groups.</i>

00:53.320 --> 00:55.820
<i>They're both ready to show their strength,</i>

00:55.820 --> 00:58.320
<i>and are proving it by winning every match thus far.</i>

00:55.820 --> 00:58.320
OTOMO MIDDLE SCHOOL

00:58.320 --> 01:00.120
Falcon...

01:00.680 --> 01:02.000
Shot!

01:07.250 --> 01:08.250
All right!

01:08.250 --> 01:10.250
He did it!

01:08.250 --> 01:12.760
SIGN: SEMI-FINAL
OTOMO MIDDLE SCHOOL: 5 - 0 : KAWAZUICHI MIDDLE SCHOOL

01:09.160 --> 01:12.760
<i>The first team to advance in the bracket is Otomo Middle School,</i>

01:12.760 --> 01:14.510
<i>followed shortly by Nankatsu.</i>

01:14.510 --> 01:15.430
Here!

01:16.100 --> 01:16.590
Taki!

01:17.960 --> 01:18.470
Kisugi!

01:19.780 --> 01:24.890
<i>Defeating Okabe Middle School 5-1 in the semi-final, Nankatsu advanced to the finals.</i>

01:22.560 --> 01:24.890
SIGN: SEMI-FINAL
NANKATSU MIDDLE SCHOOL: 5 - 1 : OKABE MIDDLE SCHOOL

01:25.910 --> 01:27.060
That's Nankatsu for you.

01:27.060 --> 01:30.360
Their moves are flawless and there's no holes in their formation.

01:30.360 --> 01:34.260
Tsubasa is at their core, and they have Izawa, Taki and Kisugi on the offensive.

01:34.260 --> 01:38.000
And on their defense, they have Morisaki, Takasugi and Ishizaki.

01:38.820 --> 01:43.580
Even if they look like a flawless, perfect team, in the end, it all comes down to Tsubasa.

01:43.580 --> 01:48.580
Their attack and defense are only possible after Tsubasa wins the ball and directs them.

01:48.580 --> 01:52.590
So, as long as we can keep Tsubasa pinned, we can surely win.

01:52.590 --> 01:54.460
You are exactly right.

01:55.340 --> 02:00.450
However, just pinning Tsubasa down is the most difficult thing.

02:00.450 --> 02:01.400
You are...

02:01.400 --> 02:02.890
Kojiro Hyuga!

02:02.890 --> 02:09.900
Thanks to him, I've been the runner-up for the past two years, so I know this all too well.

02:09.900 --> 02:12.520
But this year will be different!

02:13.170 --> 02:18.050
This year, Toho Academy is a superior team to Nankatsu!

02:18.050 --> 02:21.530
In football, the team with the highest overall strength wins.

02:21.530 --> 02:25.500
I will prove that by finally winning the champion's title this year!

02:25.500 --> 02:26.760
Oh, is that so?

02:26.760 --> 02:30.960
But we, Otomo, will crush Nankatsu first!

02:32.290 --> 02:33.830
That's impossible!

02:33.830 --> 02:39.200
I've seen you play, and I can say that defeating Nankatsu is still a distant dream for you!

02:39.200 --> 02:39.970
What did you say?

02:39.970 --> 02:41.810
Hey, Hyuga...

02:41.810 --> 02:45.380
Say that after you've become the national champion at least once.

02:45.380 --> 02:46.470
What?!

02:46.470 --> 02:49.870
Just saying. I've done it before.

02:49.870 --> 02:56.030
I defeated your favorite pupil, Takeshi Sawada,
on my way to becoming champion.

02:56.030 --> 02:58.190
My name is Shun Nitta!

02:58.190 --> 02:59.740
Remember it!

03:04.220 --> 03:06.930
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

03:04.220 --> 03:06.930
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

03:07.850 --> 03:10.520
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

03:07.850 --> 03:10.520
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

03:11.440 --> 03:14.150
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

03:11.440 --> 03:14.150
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

03:21.020 --> 03:23.870
<i>moeru you ni hitori demo</i>

03:21.020 --> 03:23.870
<i>I keep running, lying to myself</i>

03:23.870 --> 03:30.120
<i>ikiteyukeru to usobuite hashiritsudzukete</i>

03:23.870 --> 03:30.120
<i>that I can live alone, though the loneliness makes me burn</i>

03:30.120 --> 03:36.000
<i>unubore no morosa wo kimi wa shitteta no ni</i>

03:30.120 --> 03:36.000
<i>You knew how fragile my self-conceit makes me</i>

03:36.000 --> 03:42.590
<i>kokoro made uchinomaresareta kono yoru ni</i>

03:36.000 --> 03:42.590
<i>In this night that even shattered my heart</i>

03:42.590 --> 03:46.600
<i>kimi no koe sagasu</i>

03:42.590 --> 03:46.600
<i>I hate how weak I am</i>

03:46.600 --> 03:51.100
<i>kono yowasa ga nikui yo</i>

03:46.600 --> 03:51.100
<i>yearning for your voice</i>

03:51.100 --> 03:56.650
<i>ima sugu torimodoshi ni ikanakya</i>

03:51.100 --> 03:56.650
<i>"I've got to get you back right now!"</i>

03:56.650 --> 03:58.230
<i>baka darou?</i>

03:56.650 --> 03:58.230
<i>I'm stupid, right?</i>

03:58.230 --> 03:59.440
<i>ai</i>

03:58.230 --> 03:59.440
<i>Love!</i>

03:59.440 --> 04:03.070
<i>kizudarake no ai wo shinjite</i>

03:59.440 --> 04:03.070
<i>Believing in my scarred love</i>

04:03.070 --> 04:12.830
<i>nagareochita namida sae mo tsuyosa e to kaete</i>

04:03.070 --> 04:12.830
<i>I will turn these shedded tears into strength</i>

04:12.830 --> 04:13.670
<i>ai</i>

04:12.830 --> 04:13.670
<i>Love!</i>

04:13.670 --> 04:17.460
<i>kizudarake no ai da to shite mo</i>

04:13.670 --> 04:17.460
<i>Even though it is a scarred love</i>

04:17.460 --> 04:21.470
<i>bokura no sekai wo tomoshiteru</i>

04:17.460 --> 04:21.470
<i>it lightens up our world</i>

04:21.470 --> 04:27.720
<i>kono ai mo ichido taritomo</i>

04:21.470 --> 04:27.720
<i>I will not let go of this love</i>

04:27.720 --> 04:30.510
<i>hanasanai</i>

04:27.720 --> 04:30.510
<i>for a single moment!</i>

04:32.250 --> 04:37.250
<b><b>EPISODE 30:
PREFECTURAL TOURNAMENT FINALS!
FALCON SHOT APPEARS!</b></b>

04:37.850 --> 04:39.920
Good morning!

04:39.920 --> 04:41.670
Good morning, Kumi!

04:41.670 --> 04:45.640
It's almost time for the finals, Nakazawa.

04:45.640 --> 04:47.680
If we win, we'll go to the Nationals.

04:47.680 --> 04:50.680
I'll cheer for them with all I've got today as well!

04:51.270 --> 04:52.900
What's that?

04:53.560 --> 04:56.810
I cut the lemons in slices and put them in honey.

04:56.810 --> 04:59.090
I thought it'd be good to eat during half-time.

04:59.090 --> 05:00.980
Are they for Tsubasa?

05:00.980 --> 05:02.940
No... F-for everyone...

05:02.940 --> 05:04.500
As expected of Nakazawa!

05:04.500 --> 05:06.380
It's really hot outside.

05:06.380 --> 05:09.600
You'll be feeding Tsubasa lemons when he comes back all beat up!

05:09.600 --> 05:11.480
His fatigue from the first half will be gone!

05:11.480 --> 05:13.500
<i>"Yes! Let's do this in the second half!"</i>

05:14.250 --> 05:15.500
<i>"Shoot!"</i>

05:15.500 --> 05:16.660
<i>"Goal!"</i>

05:16.660 --> 05:17.780
What are you doing?

05:19.740 --> 05:21.080
Come on, let's go.

05:21.080 --> 05:22.710
Yes!

05:22.710 --> 05:26.220
<i>The Shizuoka Prefectural Tournament grand finals are about to start.</i>

05:26.220 --> 05:32.270
<i>The stadium is full, and a fierce cheering battle is already unfolding in the stands!</i>

05:30.670 --> 05:33.210
Otomo Middle School, fight!

05:36.600 --> 05:39.110
We can finally see Tsubasa Ozora.

05:39.110 --> 05:42.150
Yeah, finally.

05:42.780 --> 05:44.400
Listen, guys.

05:44.400 --> 05:49.660
We may have not had any trouble winning so far, but today's match with Otomo will be a little different.

05:49.660 --> 05:52.600
I want you to be more careful than usual today.

05:52.600 --> 05:53.490
Yes!

05:53.490 --> 05:55.430
Coach!

05:55.430 --> 05:56.660
What is it, Tsubasa?

05:56.660 --> 06:02.000
Will you let me play as a defensive midfielder in the defensive half and mark Nitta today?

06:02.000 --> 06:03.720
Mark Nitta?

06:03.720 --> 06:04.520
Yes.

06:04.520 --> 06:07.240
Urabe and his team will firmly protect Otomo's goal,

06:07.240 --> 06:10.050
and they often counterattack with Nitta.

06:10.050 --> 06:13.430
If I prioritize attacking and go on the offensive as usual,

06:13.430 --> 06:17.850
I'll be leaving Nitta open and doing exactly what our opponent wants.

06:17.850 --> 06:22.610
Also, Nitta is very serious about challenging me.

06:22.610 --> 06:25.400
I want to accept his challenge and face him!

06:26.360 --> 06:28.990
Understood. Let's use Tsubasa's tactic.

06:28.990 --> 06:30.720
Are you okay with it, guys?

06:30.720 --> 06:31.820
Yes!

06:32.330 --> 06:37.040
We've been working hard this year, aiming to bring down Nankatsu, the reigning champions.

06:37.040 --> 06:41.700
Today, the time to realize our goal has finally arrived.

06:41.700 --> 06:42.940
Listen, guys.

06:42.940 --> 06:46.170
As we are now, we can definitely defeat Nankatsu!

06:46.170 --> 06:50.500
We'll finally defeat Nankatsu this year and participate in the National Tournament!

06:50.500 --> 06:51.300
Yes!

06:53.540 --> 06:56.640
<i>Both teams are coming out onto the field.</i>

06:56.640 --> 06:59.120
Our goal differential has been the same so far.

06:59.120 --> 07:01.060
This match will be our duel.

07:01.060 --> 07:03.520
<i>The stadium suddenly fires up!</i>

07:03.520 --> 07:06.360
Otomo! Defeat Nankatsu this year!

07:06.360 --> 07:10.150
<i>Neither team has changed their lineup
since the first game, fielding their best.</i>

07:10.150 --> 07:14.260
<i>Who will win the prefectural tournament and to go to the Nationals?</i>

07:14.260 --> 07:17.180
<i>Both schools have been contenders for the title from the start.</i>

07:17.180 --> 07:19.120
<i>We're looking forward to this game!</i>

07:19.700 --> 07:24.340
<i>As you might know, most of the regular players of both teams</i>

07:24.340 --> 07:28.880
<i>were teammates in Nankatsu during elementary school.</i>

07:28.880 --> 07:32.890
<i>Moreover, Otomo's Nitta became Nankatsu SC's captain after Tsubasa,</i>

07:32.890 --> 07:40.140
<i>winning the National Youth Football Tournament along with the goalkeeper, Ichijo.</i>

07:40.140 --> 07:43.270
<i>You can call this match a fated showdown.</i>

07:43.270 --> 07:46.020
<i>Will the invincible Nankatsu win?</i>

07:46.020 --> 07:48.150
<i>Or will upstart Otomo emerge victorious?</i>

07:50.110 --> 07:53.450
<i>The final of the Shizuoka Prefectural Tournament kicks-off!</i>

07:53.450 --> 07:56.450
<i>Kisugi and Izawa close in on the opponent's side.</i>

07:56.450 --> 07:59.540
<i>Will playmaker Tsubasa come forward too?</i>

08:00.080 --> 08:01.490
<i>No, he doesn't move.</i>

08:01.490 --> 08:04.290
<i>Tsubasa remains a little further back.</i>

08:04.290 --> 08:05.130
What?

08:05.130 --> 08:06.420
What does this mean?

08:06.420 --> 08:08.300
Won't Tsubasa attack?

08:08.300 --> 08:11.920
We'll be enough for you even if Tsubasa doesn't come.

08:11.920 --> 08:13.050
What did you say?

08:14.050 --> 08:14.720
Let's go!

08:14.720 --> 08:15.690
Yeah!

08:15.690 --> 08:19.220
<i>Nankatsu begin their attack with Kisugi, Taki and Izawa!</i>

08:19.220 --> 08:20.470
Don't underestimate us!

08:21.270 --> 08:22.700
<i>That's right.</i>

08:22.700 --> 08:26.520
<i>Us setting our sights on just defeating Nankatsu so far</i>

08:26.520 --> 08:28.760
<i>was because of you!</i>

08:28.760 --> 08:34.450
<i>Even when we were in Nankatsu SC, no matter how you look at it, us four have always remained in the shadows!</i>

08:34.450 --> 08:40.290
<i>And yet, you were chosen as MVPs during the Youth Football Tournament.</i>

08:40.290 --> 08:44.540
That's right! I have turned that inferiority complex
into strength all these years!

08:44.540 --> 08:46.920
We'll let you have a taste of your own medicine!

08:46.920 --> 08:48.420
We will win!

08:48.420 --> 08:50.050
Let's go Nankatsu!

08:50.050 --> 08:52.130
Like hell we'd let you get one over us!

08:52.130 --> 08:53.670
Taki!

08:56.720 --> 08:58.720
<i>Otomo Middle School steals the ball!</i>

08:58.720 --> 08:59.970
What?!

08:59.970 --> 09:05.560
<i>The keystones of Otomo's defense, Urabe, Nishio, Kishida and Nakayama form the Otomo Quartet!</i>

09:05.560 --> 09:07.620
<i>Their moves are truly exquisite!</i>

09:07.620 --> 09:09.820
Is this how strong they are now?

09:09.820 --> 09:11.300
We'll stop them!

09:11.300 --> 09:12.320
Yeah!

09:12.320 --> 09:13.740
In your dreams!

09:15.110 --> 09:17.280
<i>Otomo sends a pass!</i>

09:17.280 --> 09:21.290
<i>The pass directly reaches the center forward, Nitta!</i>

09:21.290 --> 09:22.950
Nice pass!

09:22.950 --> 09:24.080
Like I'd let you!

09:26.170 --> 09:27.210
What?

09:27.210 --> 09:32.840
<i>Nitta, who can run 100 meters in 11 seconds, uses his speed and dashes to the goal!</i>

09:32.840 --> 09:35.590
All right! Let's start with a goal!

09:35.590 --> 09:38.590
<i>However Nankatsu's captain Tsubasa goes to mark him!</i>

09:38.590 --> 09:41.600
Is this why Tsubasa stayed behind?

09:41.600 --> 09:42.760
<i>So, you have come!</i>

09:42.760 --> 09:45.100
<i>I've been waiting for this moment!</i>

09:45.100 --> 09:46.590
<i>Come, Nitta.</i>

09:46.590 --> 09:48.850
<i>I accept your challenge.</i>

09:48.850 --> 09:53.940
wild birb speak. I can't tell the difference between wild birbs no, they are enemy stand

10:00.280 --> 10:03.870
<i>They clash straight on!</i>

10:08.660 --> 10:11.750
<i>The more experienced Tsubasa comes away with the ball!</i>

10:11.750 --> 10:13.300
Crap!

10:13.300 --> 10:15.340
Let's attack with this!

10:15.340 --> 10:17.340
Damn you, Tsubasa Ozora!

10:17.340 --> 10:19.340
The real show starts now!

10:19.340 --> 10:21.340
As expected from Tsubasa Ozora.

10:21.340 --> 10:23.140
Those are some nice moves.

10:23.140 --> 10:24.350
You're right.

10:24.350 --> 10:25.520
Come, Tsubasa!

10:25.520 --> 10:28.020
This won't be any fun if you don't come at me!

10:28.020 --> 10:31.810
<i>The Otomo Quartet is waiting for Tsubasa.</i>

10:31.810 --> 10:36.840
<i>We've bet everything on defeating Nankatsu—
on defeating Tsubasa for the past year.</i>

10:36.840 --> 10:39.820
<i>In order to be able to keep up with Tsubasa's speed...</i>

10:39.820 --> 10:42.700
<i>In order to be able to react to all of his tricks...</i>

10:42.700 --> 10:45.700
<i>We've relentlessly trained throughout the year!</i>

10:45.700 --> 10:48.260
<i>Even if we are not as gifted as you are in football,</i>

10:48.260 --> 10:51.210
<i>we won't lose to you in effort and hard work!</i>

10:51.210 --> 10:54.300
We'll show you the fruits of our training, Tsubasa!

10:54.300 --> 10:56.090
Get past us if you can!

10:56.090 --> 10:57.780
<i>I'll break through this time.</i>

10:57.780 --> 10:59.510
<i>I'll be sure to pay you back!</i>

11:00.110 --> 11:02.850
<i>This is a head-on duel!</i>

11:06.980 --> 11:07.600
<i>I've got it!</i>

11:09.140 --> 11:12.520
<i>Did Tsubasa's leg get caught up? He loses his balance!</i>

11:12.520 --> 11:13.230
Tsubasa!

11:16.140 --> 11:17.110
Tsubasa?

11:17.110 --> 11:19.850
What happened? What was that move?

11:19.850 --> 11:22.200
Their opponent is pretty good too.

11:22.200 --> 11:22.870
What?

11:22.870 --> 11:29.120
If Tsubasa tried to dribble past, he'd surely get the ball stolen from him.

11:29.120 --> 11:31.440
<i>Their reflexes are too sharp.</i>

11:31.440 --> 11:34.790
<i>They blocked every path I could use with their movement.</i>

11:34.790 --> 11:36.380
<i>That's befitting of you.</i>

11:36.380 --> 11:40.640
<i>You noticed our play and quickly decided to pass it back, instead.</i>

11:40.640 --> 11:42.670
All right! We go for Ishizaki this time!

11:42.670 --> 11:43.800
Yeah!

11:42.670 --> 11:43.310
Yeah!

11:43.310 --> 11:43.800
What?!

11:43.800 --> 11:45.800
If Tsubasa can't do it, it's impossible for me!

11:46.930 --> 11:48.760
Tsubasa's falling back!

11:48.760 --> 11:49.850
Now's our chance now!

11:51.420 --> 11:52.060
Oda!

11:55.080 --> 11:55.940
Takasugi!

11:56.560 --> 12:01.070
<i>Last year's champion Nankatsu is losing their ground despite keeping the ball!</i>

12:01.070 --> 12:02.180
See that?

12:02.180 --> 12:05.320
If you just hold Tsubasa down, this is the team you get!

12:05.320 --> 12:06.800
Damn...

12:06.800 --> 12:09.080
Guys! Don't get swept by their pace.

12:09.080 --> 12:10.930
Focus on getting the ball back to Tsubasa!

12:10.930 --> 12:12.000
Yeah!

12:12.000 --> 12:14.330
<i>Nankatsu sends the ball to Tsubasa!</i>

12:15.560 --> 12:18.540
<i>Will they go on a Tsubasa-centered counterattack from here?</i>

12:18.540 --> 12:19.670
Come, Tsubasa!

12:19.670 --> 12:20.460
Izawa!

12:20.460 --> 12:23.130
<i>It's a long pass that barely beats the offside line!</i>

12:23.130 --> 12:24.390
I won't let you!

12:24.390 --> 12:27.430
<i>However, it looks like Otomo's Nakayama will cut this pass.</i>

12:28.160 --> 12:28.850
What?!

12:28.890 --> 12:32.140
<i>The ball curves in mid-air!</i>

12:32.720 --> 12:33.640
Go!

12:33.640 --> 12:36.400
<i>Tsubasa has seen through Nakayama cutting the pass,</i>

12:36.400 --> 12:38.770
<i>and sent the pass with a slight curve!</i>

12:38.770 --> 12:40.270
You did it, Tsubasa!

12:40.270 --> 12:41.780
<i>Damn you, Nakayama!</i>

12:41.780 --> 12:44.360
<i>That's what you get for underestimating Tsubasa!</i>

12:44.360 --> 12:48.200
<i>Izawa has the ball and no marker; he's shooting!</i>

12:49.870 --> 12:51.330
Okay, we've got this!

12:52.240 --> 12:53.440
<i>He caught it!</i>

12:53.440 --> 12:57.840
<i>Otomo's goalkeeper Ichijo blocks this one with a diving catch!</i>

12:57.840 --> 12:59.460
It can't be...

13:02.460 --> 13:06.890
We've made it to the finals. Finally, it's my time to shine!

13:15.020 --> 13:20.230
<i>Ichijo saves Otomo from danger with his super catch!</i>

13:20.230 --> 13:21.570
Good job, Ichijo!

13:21.570 --> 13:23.870
I can't believe he caught the shot from there.

13:23.870 --> 13:29.030
Every shot Izawa took while unmarked
would result in a goal this tournament.

13:29.030 --> 13:30.500
Aw, it was so close!

13:30.500 --> 13:32.810
I thought he scored for sure.

13:32.810 --> 13:35.770
It seems the opponent's goalkeeper is also good at his job.

13:35.770 --> 13:39.000
Nankatsu might lose this match, y'know

13:39.000 --> 13:42.550
Wait! What do you mean by that?

13:42.550 --> 13:44.300
Oh, Hiroshi!

13:45.130 --> 13:46.340
Yukari!

13:46.340 --> 13:48.380
It's really you, Hiroshi.

13:48.380 --> 13:49.920
Why are you here?

13:49.920 --> 13:51.350
Are you really asking me that?

13:51.350 --> 13:54.000
I'm here to watch Nankatsu's match, y'know.

13:54.000 --> 13:56.580
Yukari, I should be asking you the same, y'know.

13:56.580 --> 13:59.770
I'm one of Nankatsu Middle School Football Club's managers.

13:59.770 --> 14:02.910
Yukari, do you know him?

14:02.910 --> 14:04.650
Let me introduce him.

14:04.650 --> 14:08.340
Hailing from Kyushu, my cousin, football player Hiroshi Jito.

14:08.340 --> 14:09.320
Yup.

14:09.320 --> 14:10.150
So...

14:10.150 --> 14:12.380
Explain yourself! What about Nankatsu losing?

14:12.380 --> 14:13.080
Yes, yes!

14:13.080 --> 14:14.830
I meant exactly what I said, y'know.

14:14.830 --> 14:18.240
We are here to see the strength of Nankatsu,

14:18.240 --> 14:22.290
but their opponent, Otomo Middle School looks pretty good as well.

14:22.970 --> 14:25.340
The quartet that Tsubasa couldn't pass through.

14:25.340 --> 14:30.590
Also, that goalkeeper caught a shot
that was otherwise considered a sure goal.

14:30.590 --> 14:34.640
They may not be so flashy, but their skills are the real deal, y'know.

14:34.640 --> 14:38.810
I'm curious about that #9 in particular, y'know.

14:38.810 --> 14:39.850
Just as you said.

14:40.940 --> 14:43.960
Even though he clashed against Tsubasa and lost the ball,

14:43.960 --> 14:46.070
that battle was a close one.

14:46.070 --> 14:49.230
I'm sure Tsubasa's well aware of his abilities.

14:49.230 --> 14:51.030
He is marking him today.

14:51.030 --> 14:53.820
Y'know, who on the earth are you?

14:53.820 --> 14:57.750
I'm Katagiri, from the Japanese National Football Federation.

14:57.750 --> 15:03.930
And you are Hiroshi Jito, from Nagasaki representative Hirado Middle School.

15:03.930 --> 15:04.710
he said oh nein he was a big shot! inside of

15:04.710 --> 15:08.280
In this match, where both teams have focused their strength on defense,

15:08.280 --> 15:10.390
I can't expect too many goals.

15:10.390 --> 15:13.600
Therefore, the first goal will have a huge effect.

15:13.600 --> 15:16.360
With what I've seen of Otomo Middle School's keeper,

15:16.360 --> 15:19.390
Tsubasa will need to go and take a shot, himself.

15:19.390 --> 15:21.910
But, if Tsubasa were to move to attack,

15:21.910 --> 15:24.150
that #9 would become free.

15:24.150 --> 15:28.450
If we look at this situation, Otomo, whose offense and defense are better balanced,

15:28.450 --> 15:31.120
may just have the upper hand.

15:31.910 --> 15:39.330
This match is a battle between Tsubasa, who has a hefty handicap, and Otomo's #9, Shun Nitta.

15:39.330 --> 15:42.540
<i>Another pass is sent to Nitta!</i>

15:42.540 --> 15:46.330
<i>But Nankatsu's captain Tsubasa is marking him.</i>

15:46.330 --> 15:48.380
<i>Come at me, Tsubasa!</i>

15:48.830 --> 15:53.380
<i>I may not be get past you with raw strength,</i>

15:53.380 --> 15:55.850
<i>but I have other methods I can use!</i>

15:56.620 --> 15:57.260
What?!

15:57.260 --> 16:00.880
Eat this! Falcon Shot!

16:01.940 --> 16:05.560
<i>Nitta forcefully shoots!</i>

16:07.400 --> 16:10.780
<i>The ball blasts past Tsubasa and heads towards the goal!</i>

16:10.780 --> 16:11.530
Morisaki!

16:11.530 --> 16:12.110
Damn!

16:13.030 --> 16:14.100
That's it! We got it!

16:14.100 --> 16:15.700
You did it, Nitta!

16:16.450 --> 16:17.990
<i>Oh, it's off target!</i>

16:18.460 --> 16:22.120
<i>The ball barely misses! It's a close call!</i>

16:22.120 --> 16:23.100
Damn!

16:23.100 --> 16:25.130
It was just 20 centimeters off!

16:25.130 --> 16:26.630
relaxed girls and relentless bois

16:26.630 --> 16:28.150
Damn, that was scary.

16:28.150 --> 16:28.900
Sure it was.

16:28.900 --> 16:31.920
Woah! Tsubasa!

16:32.930 --> 16:35.550
I expected nothing less from you, Tsubasa.

16:35.550 --> 16:38.010
Had you run from that ball I aimed right at you,

16:38.010 --> 16:40.330
it would have certainly been a goal.

16:40.330 --> 16:46.400
Just by letting it graze you slightly, you prevented it from becoming a goal.

16:47.280 --> 16:48.610
tsubasa be lik "roflmao kek you noob ass lil bish

16:47.610 --> 16:48.610
What?!

16:49.560 --> 16:51.360
<i>You are good, Nitta.</i>

16:51.360 --> 16:52.880
<i>I am happy.</i>

16:52.880 --> 16:57.100
<i>I'm blessed to have someone who can reignite my passion for the game after so long.</i>

16:57.100 --> 16:58.700
Are you okay, Tsubasa?

16:58.700 --> 17:00.440
Coach, the first-aid kit!

17:00.440 --> 17:01.700
Sure!

17:02.650 --> 17:05.160
<i>The referee is calling for a brief cooling break.</i>

17:05.160 --> 17:07.960
<i>Both teams will be able to get something to drink.</i>

17:07.960 --> 17:09.960
He has no rivals?

17:09.960 --> 17:10.840
Yeah.

17:11.440 --> 17:14.520
Japan was too small for Tsubasa.

17:14.520 --> 17:19.680
You could say there's not a single person who can call themselves his rival.

17:20.220 --> 17:25.190
Kojiro Hyuga and Ken Wakashimazu from Toho Academy.

17:25.190 --> 17:28.040
Jun Misugi from Musashi Middle School.

17:28.040 --> 17:30.750
Hikaru Matsuyama from Furano Middle School.

17:30.750 --> 17:33.620
The Tachibana Twins from Hanawa Middle School.

17:33.620 --> 17:37.660
Back then, all of them were considered his rivals.

17:37.660 --> 17:41.110
But in these 2 years of middle school, unfortunately,

17:41.110 --> 17:44.660
none of them were able to match Tsubasa's rate of growth.

17:44.660 --> 17:50.170
To be frank, Tsubasa is already way above the high school level.

17:50.170 --> 17:57.380
And yet here, he's met a guy— unrefined as he might be—named Nitta.

17:57.380 --> 18:00.930
I'm sure the one enjoying this situation the most is Tsubasa, himself.

18:00.930 --> 18:04.350
As the one standing atop middle school football,

18:04.350 --> 18:07.390
Tsubasa needs more—and more powerful—rivals.

18:07.390 --> 18:14.530
In that aspect, Jito, you have the possibility to become his new rival too.

18:14.530 --> 18:16.200
That goes without saying, y'know!

18:16.200 --> 18:19.990
The one destroying Nankatsu's three-peat ambitions will be me, y'know!

18:19.990 --> 18:22.960
Uh, were you ever that good at football, Hiroshi?

18:22.960 --> 18:24.750
Yukari!

18:24.750 --> 18:26.910
<i>The cooling break is over!</i>

18:26.910 --> 18:28.960
<i>Both teams are returning to the field.</i>

18:30.070 --> 18:35.010
<i>The game will resume with Otomo Middle School's corner kick,</i>

18:35.010 --> 18:37.510
<i>as Tsubasa touched the ball on its way out.</i>

18:37.510 --> 18:40.390
<i>Otomo's captain Urabe will take the corner kick.</i>

18:40.390 --> 18:42.700
<i>Will he send ball to their ace, Nitta?</i>

18:42.700 --> 18:44.810
<i>Tsubasa marks him closely, though.</i>

18:46.670 --> 18:47.980
<i>It's a high ball!</i>

18:49.450 --> 18:53.020
<i>The ball is for Nakayama at the back side!</i>

18:53.020 --> 18:54.150
Morisaki, jump!

18:54.150 --> 18:55.190
Okay!

18:55.750 --> 18:59.160
<i>But Nankatsu's keeper Morisaki firmly catches it!</i>

18:59.160 --> 18:59.820
Damn!

18:59.820 --> 19:00.700
Send it to me!

19:01.260 --> 19:03.410
<i>It's Nankatsu's turn to go on offense!</i>

19:04.110 --> 19:06.120
<i>The pass reaches Izawa!</i>

19:07.040 --> 19:09.660
<i>But Otomo steals the ball immediately!</i>

19:09.660 --> 19:10.420
Urabe!

19:11.080 --> 19:11.590
Oh!

19:11.590 --> 19:15.500
<i>Otomo continues to brilliantly fend off Nankatsu's Tsubasa-less offense!</i>

19:15.500 --> 19:20.470
<i>However, with Otomo's key player Nitta marked,
they are also unable to score!</i>

19:20.470 --> 19:24.130
<i>The score for the Shizuoka Prefectural Tournament's
final match remains 0-0.</i>

19:24.130 --> 19:27.560
<i>It truly is a fierce battle for a single goal!</i>

19:27.560 --> 19:32.430
As you've said, the first goal will have a huge effect.

19:32.430 --> 19:33.190
Yeah.

19:33.190 --> 19:36.320
And as I thought, the one who will be scoring it is...

19:36.320 --> 19:39.940
<i>There's less than a minute left in the first half, and Nankatsu is on the attack.</i>

19:39.940 --> 19:42.820
<i>Otomo Middle School's defense is sturdy!</i>

19:42.820 --> 19:45.580
You can't get past us with your level of strength!

19:45.580 --> 19:48.990
Damn it! We won't be able to score unless we get past them!

19:48.990 --> 19:50.410
Like I'd let you!

19:50.410 --> 19:51.250
To the other side!

19:51.250 --> 19:52.000
Wha-!

19:52.000 --> 19:55.760
<i>Tsubasa, preoccupied with marking Nitta until now,</i>

19:55.760 --> 19:57.760
<i>finally participates in offense!</i>

19:57.760 --> 19:59.680
<i>In this fateful moment...</i>

19:59.680 --> 20:01.510
<i>You appeared, as I expected.</i>

20:03.510 --> 20:04.470
Tsubasa!

20:04.470 --> 20:06.220
<i>The ball's sent to the opposite wing!</i>

20:06.220 --> 20:07.210
Crap!

20:07.210 --> 20:10.600
<i>Otomo's Quartet are rushing to mark Tsubasa!</i>

20:11.730 --> 20:14.990
<i>Otomo's Quartet are truly awesome.</i>

20:14.990 --> 20:16.750
<i>Their movement is excellent.</i>

20:16.750 --> 20:18.980
<i>If I trap the ball here, I won't be able to shoot.</i>

20:18.980 --> 20:21.280
<i>This is the only way out!</i>

20:21.640 --> 20:22.500
What?!

20:22.500 --> 20:23.950
Is Tsubasa really...?!

20:23.950 --> 20:27.380
This is a Non-Trap Running Volley!

20:27.380 --> 20:30.000
<i>The shot is on target!</i>

20:30.000 --> 20:30.750
Ichijo!

20:32.580 --> 20:34.220
<i>It's in!</i>

20:34.220 --> 20:35.600
<i>Right corner of the goal!</i>

20:35.600 --> 20:41.300
<i>Tsubasa places the ball exactly where he wanted, with perfect control!</i>

20:41.800 --> 20:44.800
<i>Nankatsu scores their first in the 29th minute of the first half!</i>

20:44.800 --> 20:47.050
All right! I scored the first goal!

20:47.050 --> 20:51.040
That's it! We are one step closer to victory!

20:51.040 --> 20:54.020
<i>Nankatsu Middle School's cheering squad goes wild with this goal!</i>

20:54.020 --> 20:58.320
<i>A brilliant long volley shot from Tsubasa, I must say!</i>

20:58.320 --> 21:02.010
<i>This is the first goal Otomo Middle School has conceded this tournament.</i>

21:02.010 --> 21:02.820
Damn it!

21:04.300 --> 21:06.450
<i>And the whistle signals the end of the first half!</i>

21:07.060 --> 21:10.680
<i>In the Prefectural Tournament's final match, previous year's champion</i>

21:10.680 --> 21:13.460
<i>Nankatsu heads to the locker room, leading Otomo by a goal.</i>

21:13.460 --> 21:16.620
He's an awesome guy, y'know? This Tsubasa Ozora.

21:16.620 --> 21:19.420
I didn't expect him to shoot without letting the ball land.

21:19.420 --> 21:23.190
I bet the goalkeeper didn't see that shot coming, either.

21:23.190 --> 21:25.020
I'll note that right away.

21:25.020 --> 21:25.970
Yeah.

21:25.970 --> 21:30.470
<i>Precise decision-making, keeping the remaining time in consideration.</i>

21:30.470 --> 21:34.260
<i>Even if it hadn't been a goal, the first half would be over.</i>

21:34.260 --> 21:37.980
<i>He brilliantly capitalized on the only time he could leave Nitta unmarked.</i>

21:38.670 --> 21:41.860
<i>To that, I can only say "you did what you always do, Tsubasa."</i>

21:41.860 --> 21:45.860
Damn it, so it was Tsubasa by himself who got us, after all.

21:45.900 --> 21:51.060
<i>However, just pinning Tsubasa down is the most difficult thing.</i>

21:51.440 --> 21:55.580
But we've trained very hard with the
sole goal of being able to beat Tsubasa.

21:55.580 --> 21:57.960
We won't let it end like this.

21:57.960 --> 22:00.460
We will certainly turn this around in the second half!

22:02.590 --> 22:04.490
<i>That's ridiculous.</i>

22:04.490 --> 22:11.010
<i>How was he able to score with that ball, without trapping it, and from that long a range?</i>

22:11.600 --> 22:14.920
<i>But... it's the only time he's scored.</i>

22:14.920 --> 22:16.430
<i>So to win this match...!</i>

22:38.750 --> 22:44.800
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.750 --> 22:44.800
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.800 --> 22:50.800
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.800 --> 22:50.800
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.800 --> 22:56.850
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.800 --> 22:56.850
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.850 --> 23:01.480
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.850 --> 23:01.480
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:03.110 --> 23:07.770
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:03.110 --> 23:07.770
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.110 --> 23:15.200
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.110 --> 23:15.200
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:15.200 --> 23:21.250
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.250 --> 23:25.710
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.250 --> 23:25.710
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:27.010 --> 23:33.340
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:27.010 --> 23:33.340
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.340 --> 23:39.390
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.390 --> 23:45.690
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.390 --> 23:45.690
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:49.990 --> 24:00.630
COMING UP, EPISODE 31:
FALCON VS. TSUBASA
